# Predictor recovery under calls and returns: a data-dependent branch inside a called
# function mispredicts repeatedly, so wrong paths speculatively pop and push the RAS
# and shift the GHR. The architectural result must be exact regardless of predictor
# state (ADR-019 D-19.11: predictor state is microarchitectural); the FTQ must release
# and train every committed block in order.
@name ooo-call-return-recovery
@verifies funcFtqRecovery propFtqRecoveryKeepsOlder funcFtqAllocate funcFtqFetchIssue funcFtqCommitTrain
@verifies propFtqInOrderRelease funcBlockEndCommit funcFetchPcSelect propFetchPcAligned funcFetchBufferEnqueue
@verifies funcFetchPacketDequeue propFetchBufferProgramOrder propFetchInOrder propNoStaleFetchBlock funcFetchGeneration
@verifies funcPredictionCheck propBranchCompletesOnce
@maxcycles 20000
li x5, 0
li x6, 0
li x8, 16
loop: jal x1, func
addi x6, x6, 1
bne x6, x8, loop
check x5 == 40
jal x0, end
func: andi x7, x6, 1
beq x7, x0, evenpath
addi x5, x5, 1
evenpath: addi x5, x5, 2
jalr x0, x1, 0
end: addi x0, x0, 0
